The Shrewd Dude schrieb:
> 
> TRIVIA SET #101:

> 1. This member of the ape-like creatures gives its name to the group
> symbol 'Y'.

The Sas - no, wait, the Yeti.

> 2. Fungi and jellies usually have what type of attack?

"Defensive attacks" - you suffer effects when you touch them.
Exceptions are the Shrieker and Violet Fungus.

> 3. Are the symbol for a soldier and the symbol for a priest the same?

Only on a monochrome display: on colour terminals, soldiers are grey,
priests white. They use the same typographical symbol, though.

> 4. This food abuses your wisdom and makes you nauseous.

Dunno. Rotten meat from a tin?

> 5. What is the 'special' spell for rangers?

Ignite Ringwraith?

> 6. This is the other food that nauseates.

Rotten egg.

> 7. As a Valkyrie, will you ever suddenly feel very cold?

Only if you lose your cold resistance to a gremlin attack.

> 8. Name the colors that an 'L' might appear in.

Any, as long as you're hallucinating.
Brown, red, purple, white when not hallucinating - white for 'L's in
text.
Green when playing on an ancient monochrome terminal.

> 9. There are these many members of the 'N' group.

Either four or eight, depending on whether you look at actual species
or entries in the monster list, which counts hatchlings and adults
separately.

> 10. These creatures carry white-handed shields.

Uruk-hai; they can also be _carried_ by creatures who chose them as
equipment, by gelatinous cubes, by nymphs and by your little dog.

> 11. Kobolds are known for carrying these weapons.

The often carry darts.

> 12. True or false: The Wizard of Yendor doesn't know how to use a
> weapon.

True.

> 13. True or false: As a gnomish Healer, eating a Healer corpse is
> considered cannabalism.

False.
There's no such thing as 'cannabalism'.

> 14. True or false: A mimic can ooze under doors.

True.
Sort of - a mimic can move into the square occupied by a closed door.

> 15. Tossing a gem to a non-aligned unicorn can change your luck in how
> many ways?

Two - it can either raise or lower your luck.

> 16. A faded pall is the description for what type of item?

Elven cloak.

> 19. A hard hat is the description for what type of item?

Dwarven helm.

> 20. True or false: Trying to genocide the 'A' group will have the same
> result as trying to genocide 'E'.

No. You can genocide stalkers.

> 21. There are these many members in the 'V' group.

At most 241 members of the group can be generated per game.

> 22. When can you see the image of someone stalking you?

When gaining see invisible by drinking from a fountain.

> 23. True or false: Humans can safely eat Quantum Mechanics, Stalkers,
> and Kops.

False. Totally false: one corpse is poisonous, the other causes
stunning, eating the third will be considered cannibalism.

> 24. If you see a red ;, what creature(s) might it be?

Any when hallucinating.
Other than that, either piranha or kraken.

> 25. True or false: Gray Oozes can damage your armour.

True, their bite corrodes metal items.

